1208		Under the diagonal line-point law, the probability of a zero direction is
1209		at most $1/q$. Under the equal mixture of axis-parallel and diagonal laws it
1210		is at most $1/(2q)$. Hence, for two independent line-point samples, removing
1211		the event that the $X$-line has zero direction discards mass at most
1212		$1/(2q)$.
1213	\end{lemma}
