1326			\mathrm{combine}_{f,g}(u + t \cdot v)
1327			= (u_\alpha + t \cdot v_\alpha)\, f(u_X + t \cdot v_X)
1328			+ (u_\beta + t \cdot v_\beta)\, g(u_Z + t \cdot v_Z)\,,
1329			\qquad t \in \F_q\,.
1330		\end{equation}
1331		The degree bound holds because $f$ and $g$, restricted to lines, are
1332		polynomials of degree at most $md$ in the line parameter, and each is
1333		multiplied by an affine factor of degree at most one.
